{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":115524,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"20073dbe-c3a4-424d-8011-48337dc05844","total_cost_usd":0.6861714999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40006,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":10130,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10130,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":24273,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.024368,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10130,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40006,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6618035,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\":     { \"slots_crushed\": 1, \"slots_uncrushed\": 2, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"medium\":    { \"slots_crushed\": 2, \"slots_uncrushed\": 4, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"oversized\": { \"slots_crushed\": 6, \"slots_uncrushed\": 12, \"hand_tetherable\": false }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 34.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A buckled length of lattice strut off a launch adapter; the honest bread-and-butter haul of the low sky, heavy enough to teach towing but too dull to be worth a detour.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Plate\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 12.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"Curved skin panel with one edge already burned brown by a pass it survived; the most common thing in the sky and the piece the player learns the hand magnet on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_booster_ring\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Booster Ring\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 28.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"The interstage collar left when somebody else staged; solid metal, crushes flat, and reads instantly as the same kind of part the player just threw away.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tangled_wiring_loom\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tangled Wiring Loom\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 6.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A knot of harness cable and connectors; nearly free to tow, which makes it the piece worth grabbing on the way past rather than the piece worth crossing for.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_antenna_dish\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Antenna Dish\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 9.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A dented comms dish that still glints on its slow tumble; the player's first fragile piece, cheap enough in mass that the lesson costs only patience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insulation_blanket_wad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Insulation Blanket Wad\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 4.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"Balled-up gold foil MLI, almost weightless on the tether; the piece that proves slot cost and mass cost are different currencies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fairing_shard\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fairing Shard\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 8.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A composite splinter of nose cone with the paint still on it; easy filler that keeps a light run from coming home empty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"camera_optics_pod\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Camera Optics Pod\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 5.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"An intact imaging head with the lens somehow unbroken; light, delicate, and the cheapest possible rehearsal for the glass the player will chase higher up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 180.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A dead kick stage tumbling end over end; crane-cable only, so it hangs there all semester as a visible promise of a tool the player does not own yet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"satellite_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Satellite Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 62.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The gutted skeleton of a comms satellite; the low band's staple and the first piece heavy enough that a second tether visibly changes how the jetpack answers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 48.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A sealed flywheel can, dense for its size and still faintly spinning; solid enough to shrug off a bad landing, which makes it the safe half of a mixed haul.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 22.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded wing of cells with a spiderweb fracture across one panel; the signature fragile prize of the shipping slice — light to tow, ruinous to land hard.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fuel_tank_bladder\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fuel Tank Bladder\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 18.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A collapsed propellant bladder still weeping frozen hydrazine; compact, forgiving, and the low band's answer to a hold with one slot left.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gyro_package\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gyro Package\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 26.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A machined inertial unit the size of a toolbox and heavier than it looks; the piece that teaches that small is a slot cost, not a mass promise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 11.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head that catches the sun on a slow cycle; small, precious, and usually parked out on its own orbit a real burn away from the clump.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thruster_quad_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Thruster Quad Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 55.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"Four scorched RCS nozzles on a common manifold; heavy, tough, and the load the player is towing when they first feel a cable come taut on a turn.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dish_reflector_petal\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dish Reflector Petal\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 19.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A mesh reflector segment that never folds flat and never crushes; light on the tether but it eats four uncrushed slots, so taking it is a decision about the hold, not the jetpack.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Boom Mast\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 330.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescoping mast jammed half-extended, longer than the rocket; crane-cable only, and the practice rendezvous for the capstone if the crane ever ships.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rtg_core_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"RTG Core Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 96.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A shielded isotope generator casing, still warm to the glove; the high band's workhorse and the clearest statement that up here the good stuff fights you on the way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tungsten_ballast_slug\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tungsten Ballast Slug\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 84.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A trim mass the size of a brick and the weight of a person; one crushed slot, and it will still ruin a parachute descent all by itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_optics_mirror\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Optics Mirror\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 44.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A primary mirror segment with a crazed coating that throws light every few seconds; the glint the player sees from a band away and has to talk themselves into.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_tank_segment\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Tank Segment\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 78.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A vacuum-jacketed tank barrel frosted white; solid, dense, and exactly the ballast that turns a one-pass reentry into a three-pass one.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ion_engine_gridset\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Ion Engine Gridset\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 21.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"Paper-thin accelerator grids in a scorched frame; the lightest thing in the top band and the easiest of its prizes to lose to a hot pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardened_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Hardened Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 52.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A rad-hard flight computer in a milled block of aluminium; the reliable high-band pickup for a player who already knows the ride home is going to be ugly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"deep_space_dish_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Deep Space Dish Array\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 58.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A rigid high-gain antenna the size of a door; fragile, uncrushable, and heavy — bulk, mass and risk in one piece, which is the top band's whole argument.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_boom_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Sensor Boom Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 68.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"An instrument arm with three magnetometer heads still bolted on; awkward on the tether, and it swings wide on every direction change the player rushes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_satellite\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Satellite\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 480.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"The one Mr. Armstrong lost on cascade day, parked above the top band — unique rather than spawned, fragile and oversized so it can only be craned, can never be crushed, and arrives broken unless the touchdown is soft.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 31.89\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.167,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 65.67\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 109.0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass carries the difficulty curve, because the Researcher established that altitude cannot: entry speed spans only 151-164 m/s across the three bands, a 1.27x heat ratio, so the return leg gets harder only if the cargo gets heavier. Band mean mass runs 31.89 / 65.67 / 109.0 kg, so a high-band piece averages about 3.4x a suborbital one; excluding the single oversized outlier in each band, the hand-tetherable population averages 13.4 / 32.6 / 62.6 kg, a 4.7x climb from bottom to top.\",\n    \"Fragile fraction is spawn-weighted, not counted: suborbital is 7 of 70 weight (0.100) across 2 of 9 pieces, low is 10 of 60 (0.167) across 3 of 9, high is 16 of 64 (0.250) across 4 of 9. Fragile types are deliberately given below-average weights within their band so that adding a fragile piece raises variety without inflating how often the player meets one.\",\n    \"Size class is authored against the fiction, never derived from mass, and two pieces exist specifically to prove that to the player: tungsten_ballast_slug is small at 84 kg and gyro_package is small at 26 kg, while cracked_solar_array is medium at 22 kg. A slot is volume and a kilogram is handling, and the catalog refuses to let those two collapse into one number.\",\n    \"The shipping slice is complete without the crane. Suborbital and low each contain small, medium and fragile pieces, so every rule the player must learn is teachable below 400 m; the three oversized pieces (one per band) carry 92 of the 981 kg... more precisely they carry 180, 330 and 480 kg at spawn weight 1 each, and are marked crane-only so the slice can ship with them visible and unreachable.\",\n    \"Higher bands skew medium as the GDD asks - 2 medium of 9 in suborbital, 5 of 9 in low and high - so slots fill faster with altitude at the same piece count. Suborbital stays small-heavy (6 of 9) so a starting hold of 6 slots can be filled by a beginner without a compactor upgrade, which is what keeps the opening loop solvable.\",\n    \"Fragile is concentrated where reach cost is highest: cracked_antenna_dish and camera_optics_pod are the cheap suborbital rehearsals, star_tracker_head and dish_reflector_petal are the low-band decisions, and shattered_optics_mirror, ion_engine_gridset and deep_space_dish_array are the top-band prizes. deep_space_dish_array is the deliberate worst case among tetherable junk - fragile, medium, and 58 kg - so the top band always offers at least one piece that is bulk, mass and risk at once.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly dominant. The heaviest tetherable pieces are non-fragile and crushable (rtg_core_shell, tungsten_ballast_slug, cryo_tank_segment), the lightest are cheap filler, and every fragile piece pays uncrushed slot cost forever - so a greedy hold and a valuable hold are different hauls, and the player has to choose which one to fly home.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":51850,"ttft_stream_ms":1455,"time_to_request_ms":264,"type":"result","duration_ms":114295,"uuid":"71fd2e4b-1d2d-458b-b6f6-ac7288337f1a"}
